      "body": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\n\n## Motivation\n\nSpeculative decoding relocates KV rows with `move_kv_cache`: accepted draft tokens are moved into place after verification (`spec_utils.py`, EAGLE with topk > 1 and NGRAM), and with page_size > 1 the prefix tail page is copied to each branch (`eagle_worker_common.py`). `MLATokenToKVPoolFP4` inherits `MLATokenToKVPool.move_kv_cache` (#26982), which copies `kv_buffer` rows only. Each moved FP4 latent is then dequantized with whatever block scales were left at its target slot, typically a rejected draft token's, and nothing reports an error.\n\nThe other quantized pools already move scales with their data (`MHATokenToKVPool`, `MHATokenToKVPoolMXFP8`, `DSATokenToKVPool`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `MLATokenToKVPoolFP4.move_kv_cache`: run the MLA move for the latent, then copy the `kv_scale_buffer` rows with the same indices.\n- `test_quantized_kv_pool.py`: a CPU `MLATokenToKVPoolFP4` test that moves two slots and checks that data and scales arrive in every layer.\n\nOut of scope: other methods inherited from `MLATokenToKVPool` also handle `kv_buffer` only (`get_cpu_copy`/`load_cpu_copy`, `get_contiguous_buf_infos`, the HiCache host pool, `get_kv_size_bytes`). As with MXFP8 (#35888, #35718), each needs its own PR.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nFound by code inspection and verified at the unit level; not reproduced end to end, which needs an MLA model served with the FP4 KV cache and EAGLE topk > 1 or NGRAM decoding. The change only moves the scale rows of slots that the existing move already relocates.\n\n- `python3 test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_quantized_kv_pool.py`: OK (2 tests). On main the new test fails at the scale assertion.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nOne extra gather and `index_put_` per layer per move, on `[n, kv_cache_dim / 16]` uint8 rows. Only moves on an FP4 MLA cache pay it.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (not needed)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (see above)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39226249602](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39226249602)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39226249240](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39226249240)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39226249467](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39226249467)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
